#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(2.8)")
 $ 1 - { k alpha_i } in \[ b_j \, 1 - b_j \] . $ <eq:spread>]

 If $G_j K_j lt.eq \| k \| lt.eq N_j \/ 4$, every index in $J_j$ has $1 - { k alpha_i } in \[ a_j \, 1 - a_j \]$.]
  #emph[The initial values are $K_1 = 100 \, G_1 = 1$. The numbers $L_j gt.eq 1$ are nondecreasing, $C_j =
    max \( L_j \, K_j^2 \)$, and the sizes satisfy
#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(2.9)")
 $ & m_j gt.eq max \( K_j \, 2^j \, 4 G_j \, 200 \) \, wide K_(j + 1) = ceil.l m_j^(\( 3 \/ 4 \) m_j) ceil.r > 2 K_j \,\
 & G_(j + 1) K_(j + 1) < m_j^(\( 4 \/ 5 \) m_j) \, wide kappa_j m_j^(1 \/ 40) gt.eq L_j \, wide
   kappa_(j + 1) sqrt(G_(j + 1)) gt.eq L_j \,\
